{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact BR-14 head d8d3662696bd9bb0b57aefbb5a4b3f1d10cc295c on builder/module-splits-br14-20261109, tree d6761191, all 25 artifacts, for request c7853c21 under promise 1d4473a5 and review request f6a93069. The split moves declarations without changing them. Public names, construction order and every runtime check stay as they were on main.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- The moves. I parsed each changed source file at the head and at main f1f6a8b9 with rolldown's `parseAst`. Every top-level declaration in the nine new CLI modules, the remaining `commands.ts`, `command-support.ts`, `worker.ts` and `worker-mcp.ts` appears verbatim in main's `commands.ts`, `command-support.ts`, `worker.ts` or `object.ts`, apart from a leading `export`. In the other direction, every declaration of main's four files appears verbatim at the head, except `ScopeObject`. `command-support.ts` changes only its type import, which now comes from `command-context.ts`.\n- The archive wiring. `object-archive.ts` holds the only new text: three helpers built from main's own statements. `configuredArchive` keeps the one-owner throw and calls `wiring.archive?.()` with `wiring` as receiver. The constructor still configures the archive, assigns `#archiveRestart`, builds the driver, then sets the floor offer. The clock, `store.scope()`, pin, transaction and discovery reads stay lazy inside callbacks. The helpers capture `#readSql`, `#scope` and `#chains` once. All three are `readonly` fields, and the constructor assigns them at lines 201, 262 and 266, before the call at line 294. The captures therefore read what `this.#…` read on main. `ArchiveDriver` becomes a type-only import in `object.ts`, and the typecheck passed.\n- The MCP cycle. `worker.ts` forwards `mcpRoute`, `McpRegistry`, `McpAgent` and the `McpEnv` type from `worker-mcp.ts`. `worker-mcp.ts` imports `route` and the `Env` type back. Its only use of `route` is inside the agent's `fetch` callback at line 239, so module initialization never reads the binding before `worker.ts` evaluates.\n- The export model. `workerEntrypoints` accepts exactly one forward from `./worker-mcp.ts`, with exactly those four names. In `worker-mcp.ts` it accepts one `cloudflare:workers` import of `DurableObject` and exactly four exported declarations: two classes on `DurableObject`, one function and one interface. It refuses any other forward, rename, alias, export-all or default export. The added controls cover each refusal, and the existing route, RPC, method, gate, body and seal controls remain.\n- The seals. Each of the 166 named seals in main's table keeps its hash under its new file. Only `ScopeObject` changes, and the three archive helpers get new seals. Each new owner has a `$module` seal. I recomputed the whole-file seal of `command-support.ts` outside the builder's worktree: 53798996…, equal to its literal.\n- The settings document. Only reader paths change, from `worker.ts` to `worker-mcp.ts`, plus the re-sorted lists from the generated lookup. No setting, kind, value, deployment or rule changes.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main f1f6a8b9 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 25 paths that its 25 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 5 checked, 0 flagged. No dependency, lockfile, Wrangler, definition, pin, migration or test-assertion file changes.\n- The gates. Gate 1 at 2ca326b5 reads `exit 1`: Node 142 passed and 2 failed, with Counting, Plain and Native unreached. It stays failed. Between 2ca326b5 and d0b362ad, only the settings document, the note and three manifests change, as ruling 33ff7a38 allows. Gate 2 at d0b362ad, tree 36d92484, reads `exit 0`: Node 144, Counting 56, Plain 4,028 plus one skip, and Native 1,124 plus two skips. After that gate, only the note and two manifests change.\n- The browsers. GitHub reports Card run 42686766157 as successful at d0b362ad. The first Card